        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the complete text of a glyph sheet, reconciled against a manifest&apos;s glyphs table. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>sheetText</computeroutput> is the existing sheet&apos;s text, or empty when no sheet exists yet. The manifest&apos;s <computeroutput>##</computeroutput> glyphs table decides which cells exist in the returned sheet: a cell present in both the table and the existing sheet keeps its own width and its artwork; a cell absent from the table is not emitted. The cells repack in table order and the canvas resizes to fit them. The parsed existing sheet is read and never modified.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>manifest</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The font family manifest, read for its glyphs and guides tables. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sheetText</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The existing sheet&apos;s text, or empty when none exists. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The complete text of the reconciled glyph sheet. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
